      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=77832914\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Medium impact]** The PR appears safe to merge; both NVFP4 view fixes match the expected storage layout.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nFixes two NVFP4 weight views in the single-group fused grouped MLP.\n- The FC1 forward scale view now uses packed K, avoiding an oversized view.\n- FC2 backward uses the shared cuDNN conversion helper with the transposed weight dimensions.\n- The single-group test now covers every available grouped MLP recipe, with existing checks for unsupported configurations.\n\nNo actionable issues were found. Tests were not run.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"\\[PyTorch\\] Fix NVFP4 weight views of the ...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/1fea5dac3f146ce3f9bc47e3fd7a3e6bf70723fa) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_expert&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=code_reviews&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
